# Build context hygiene for `docker compose build`.
#
# The Dockerfile clones structurizr/structurizr from GitHub inside the builder
# stage and does not COPY anything from this folder, so the local build context
# is essentially unused. We still ship a minimal context to keep image builds
# fast and to avoid leaking host-side state into layers if a future COPY is added.
#
# Patterns are evaluated from the build context root (this folder).

# --- Runtime data: huge and irrelevant to the image -------------------------
# Themes alone are hundreds of SVGs; the .structurizr/ index, logs, and
# workspace JSON snapshots are regenerated by the running container.
data/

# --- Host-only tooling ------------------------------------------------------
# PowerShell helpers run on the host against the running container; the image
# itself never executes them.
*.ps1

# --- VCS / IDE / OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Docs and local scratch -------------------------------------------------
# Keep the image free of READMEs, notes, and ad-hoc files that might land here.
README*
*.md
LICENSE*
NOTICE*
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*~

# --- Secrets / env files ----------------------------------------------------
# Belt-and-braces: never let a stray .env or key file slip into a layer.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.crt
secrets/

# --- Docker meta ------------------------------------------------------------
# No reason to ship the compose file or this ignore file into the image.
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
Dockerfile*
!Dockerfile
